CZsWorld and use code: CZsWorld, for 20% off&nbsp;
your first box. Again, make sure to use code:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:23.120
CZsWorld for a 20% discount and&nbsp;
to show your support for the show.

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:25.680
Can you survive the curse of The Blair Witch?

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:34.080
Fincher is a master of&nbsp;
storytelling in the subtext,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:37.440
and throughout the movie there are many&nbsp;
brilliant examples, that you may not have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.440 --> 00:06:40.960
thought about while watching. When Nick and&nbsp;
Go are playing The Game of LIFE in The Bar,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:44.720
he adds a wife to his car, but never adds&nbsp;
a child, this plays into the whole dispute&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:48.720
about Amy supposedly wanting a child, then&nbsp;
not wanting one, then wanting one again.

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:52.800
In their living room, there’s a box from a&nbsp;
brand called Piranesi. As far as I can tell,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:57.120
this isn’t a real brand, it’s likely a&nbsp;
reference to the Italian artist Piranesi,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.120 --> 00:07:01.280
who was known for his etchings of fictitious&nbsp;
and atmospheric prisons. The box is found&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:06.160
right next to the staged crime scene designed&nbsp;
by Amy to get Nick thrown in prison, or worse.

00:07:06.160 --> 00:07:08.080
As Nick takes the two detectives through the crime&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:10.800
scene, he quickly moves on from the&nbsp;
kitchen to show them the next room,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:15.760
but Boney notices the blood splatter on the&nbsp;
backsplash. This makes Nick look very suspicious.

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:20.800
Amy’s a writer, but her degree is in psychology,&nbsp;
again, setting up her mastermind of a plan.

00:07:20.908 --> 00:07:23.840
In the flashback at the release event for the new Amazing Amy book,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.840 --> 00:07:27.840
this guy is way too delighted to rub it&nbsp;
in Amy’s face that she’s not married.

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:30.000
“Because it’s my understanding&nbsp;
you are not married.”

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:32.960
Not counting that as a Thing You&nbsp;
Missed. I just find it funny.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.960 --> 00:07:36.560
The flashback of Amy and Nick’s kiss&nbsp;
cuts directly to Nick getting his cheek&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:40.000
swabbed because he’s suspected&nbsp;
of Amy’s murder. Brilliant cut.

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:44.080
In another flashback, when Amy and Nick&nbsp;
are doing the second anniversary treasure hunt at the library,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:49.040
we see a book facing the camera. Not sure if&nbsp;
it says Twin or Twain, but either way it’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.040 --> 00:07:54.160
relevant. Nick is part of a set of twins living&nbsp;
in the land of Mark Twain, I’m counting it.

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:58.640
I’m not sure how there’s a secret area of&nbsp;
this library that only they know about, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:03.760
moving on… McCaulay Culkin has a cameo for some&nbsp;
reason, it’s the kid from Home Alone. There’s a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.760 --> 00:08:08.560
theory that he’s a young John Kramer. No, I don’t&nbsp;
actually know if that’s him but it’s pretty funny.

00:08:08.560 --> 00:08:13.280
OK, moving onto a real one, the police show&nbsp;
Nick pictures of Amy with Noelle Hawthorne,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.280 --> 00:08:15.760
because Nick previously claimed&nbsp;
that she wasn’t friends with Amy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:20.400
Amy only befriended her as part of her plan, and&nbsp;
in one of these photos, they’re seen together at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:24.640
Andy’s Frozen Custard. I recognize it because we&nbsp;
used to go there after baseball games sometimes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.640 --> 00:08:28.240
I think this fits in with the idea that Amy&nbsp;
is taking Nick on a tour of shame with her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:32.400
treasure hunt. All of the clues were at places&nbsp;
that Nick was together with his mistress, Andie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:36.560
so this is another secret way of her telling&nbsp;
Nick, this is because of Andie. There’s also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.560 --> 00:08:40.240
something poetic about the fact that Amazing&nbsp;
Amy from the children’s books ends up with a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:45.440
guy named Able Andy, and the real Amy ends up with&nbsp;
a guy who cheats on her with a girl named Andie.

00:08:45.440 --> 00:08:48.160
At one point, the police ask&nbsp;
what Amy does with her time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:51.760
and he tells them she’s always got a book&nbsp;
in her hand. We later find that to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:56.320
kind of true, little does Nick know, she’s&nbsp;
actually researching her revenge on him.

00:08:56.320 --> 00:09:00.800
Later on, she’s checking in to see how everything&nbsp;
panned out and she decides to look up Ellen Abbott&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:04.720
on Google to see if she’s covered Nick on&nbsp;
her show yet. After she types the letters:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.720 --> 00:09:09.040
E-L, one of the autocomplete suggestions&nbsp;
is “Eliminate Your Spouse in Three Easy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:12.960
Steps.” And at that moment, she felt very&nbsp;
stupid. She could have done it in 3 steps,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:16.800
but instead she over complicated&nbsp;
the process to hundreds of steps.

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:20.960
Meanwhile, Nick is headed to the airport to go&nbsp;
meet with Tanner Bolt, and there’s a billboard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.960 --> 00:09:25.840
for Sharon Schieber, the other big talk show&nbsp;
host in this universe, and as Nick walks by it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.840 --> 00:09:30.560
Sharon turns almost as if to look at him -- it’s&nbsp;
like she’s eyeing him as a potential big story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.560 --> 00:09:34.960
to have on her show, and he would eventually&nbsp;
go on that show under Bolt’s recommendation.

00:09:34.960 --> 00:09:38.480
You know, I could probably forgive Nick&nbsp;
killing his wife, and I could maybe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.480 --> 00:09:44.160
even forgive him cheating on her, but this is&nbsp;just
unforgivable Nick, you’ve just lost my sympathy.

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:47.920
But right before the big Sharon Shieber&nbsp;
interview, there’s a great moment that shows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:52.400
how far Nick has come as a character. Early on he&nbsp;
was criticized for cracking a nervous smile at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:56.880
press conference for his missing wife, but by this&nbsp;
point in the story he’s become much more careful.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.880 --> 00:10:01.120
Sharon gives him this huge smile at the start of&nbsp;
the interview, and his instinct is to smile back,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:05.440
but he fights it and remains stoic. It’s a minor&nbsp;
detail, but it’s very powerful.

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:09.280
Oftentimes in Things You Missed episodes,&nbsp;
we will find that taking a closer look&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.280 --> 00:10:13.600
whenever we’re looking at text will yield&nbsp;
some good old crew-reference easter eggs.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.600 --> 00:10:16.480
There are a good amount of them, so&nbsp;
I’m gonna go through them all quickly.

00:10:16.480 --> 00:10:20.880
The Amazing Amy book illustrations by Kirk Van&nbsp;
Wormer, he’s part of Gone Girl’s art department.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:24.640
If you pause on the directory of the building&nbsp;
where Tanner Bolt’s Law Office is you’ll see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:28.560
Bolanowski Labs -- a reference to Special&nbsp;
Effects Coordinator Rob Bolanowski;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:33.120
Bradford Ralston Insurance Brokers, named&nbsp;
after sound utility man Bradford Ralston;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.120 --> 00:10:37.200
Bozeman and Associates, named after Gary&nbsp;
Bozeman of the transportation department;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:41.440
Curtis Childers and (something, you can’t make&nbsp;
the rest of it out), but Curtis Childers is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:45.360
credited as a construction foreman; Dingle&nbsp;
and George Brothers references three people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:48.560
Robert Dingle, TyRee Dingle and&nbsp;
Brett George, they all worked in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:48.560 --> 00:10:52.080
the transportation department. There&nbsp;
may be others like Brown or Campbell,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:56.000
but those are pretty common names, I’m gonna move&nbsp;
on to some more references that I’m sure about.

00:10:56.000 --> 00:10:59.600
Like the credits of the Ellen Abbott show&nbsp;
where you’ll see that Ellen Abbott’s editor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:02.560
is William Peake -- in the Gone&nbsp;
Girl credits there’s a Billy Peake&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:06.640
who was an assistant editor. Ellen’s art&nbsp;
directors are Tyler Nelson and Eric Weidt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.640 --> 00:11:10.160
an assistant editor and visual effects&nbsp;
artist on Gone Girl respectively.

00:11:10.160 --> 00:11:13.920
And lastly, Ellen Abbott’s makeup&nbsp;
department has a Chad Peter and Lyla Bol.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.920 --> 00:11:16.000
Chad is Gone Girl’s visual effect compositor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:20.320
Lyla Bol I believe is the wife of Gone Girl’s&nbsp;
post-production coordinator Randall James Bol,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:24.400
the two worked together on the second Lego&nbsp;
movie, which is Lyla’s only credit so far.

00:11:24.400 --> 00:11:29.200
At the beginning of this video, I mentioned that&nbsp;
the URL, findamazingamy.com, actually worked at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:34.480
one time, so I was curious about the phone numbers&nbsp;
as well. So I decided: I’m gonna call them.

00:11:39.120 --> 00:11:42.560
Here are a few more things I love&nbsp;
about Hunt a Killer's Blair Witch box.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.560 --> 00:11:44.880
The story. As soon as I started&nbsp;
looking over the evidence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:44.880 --> 00:11:48.080
I immediately got hooked on it. You start&nbsp;
to learn who the major characters are,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.080 --> 00:11:51.760
gain an understanding of the town, and you&nbsp;
